    "result_text": "Green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, and the audit line still shows the correct `NSW-16E6609E` identity.\n\n## What I changed\n\nI agreed with both findings and restructured accordingly.\n\n**Finding 1 \u2014 format knowledge was split.** I introduced `CustomerCode` (in `rest.function.owner`, next to `IdentityKey`), which now owns both sides of the `<REGION>-<HASH8>` format:\n- `format(region, hash8)` \u2014 used by `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`\n- `regionOf(code)` \u2014 used by `OwnerMapper` for locality\n\nThe separator and layout live in one place (a single `SEPARATOR` constant), with a javadoc rationale mirroring `IdentityKey`'s \"cannot drift apart\" note. This also removes the customerCode-format knowledge that had leaked into `Localities`, whose concern is only city/postcode\u2192region.\n\n**Finding 2 \u2014 dead, near-duplicate method.** I deleted `Localities.of(String city, String postcode)`, which had no remaining callers once locality moved off it. `ofPostcode` (the region-from-postcode path the new identity uses) and the single-arg `of` (still used by `postcodeRange`) remain.\n\nNet result: `Localities` now has three cohesive region methods instead of a fourth near-duplicate; the customerCode format is single-sourced in `CustomerCode`; and `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`/`OwnerMapper` both delegate to it. No behaviour changed \u2014 the test is still green and the emitted identity is unchanged.\n\nI had nothing to push back on; both points were consistent with the codebase's existing `IdentityKey` convention.",
